spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#dgx-spark-specific-notes","content":"Avoiding situations that make the host unusable or require long recovery"},"671":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-24","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#resource-management-is-critical","content":"Large models (70B+, MoE like Kimi-K2.6) can quickly exhaust host memory and make the node unresponsive over SSH."},"672":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-25","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#resource-management-is-critical","content":"**Rules:**"},"673":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-26","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#resource-management-is-critical","content":"Always set `resources.requests` and `resources.limits` for both CPU and memory, not just GPU."},"674":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-27","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#resource-management-is-critical","content":"Use `restartPolicy: OnFailure` with `backoffLimit: 1` for heavy jobs."},"675":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-28","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#resource-management-is-critical","content":"Prefer Jobs over Deployments for one-shot or long-running inference servers that you control explicitly."},"676":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-29","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#resource-management-is-critical","content":"Never use `imagePullPolicy: Always` on multi-hundred-GB images."},"677":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-30","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#preventing-auto-restart-on-reboot","content":"We do **not** use Deployments with high replica counts for heavy models."},"678":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-31","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#preventing-auto-restart-on-reboot","content":"We do **not** use `restartPolicy: Always` for the main inference container."},"679":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-32","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#preventing-auto-restart-on-reboot","content":"Workloads are started manually via `scripts/manage.sh`."},"680":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-33","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#preventing-auto-restart-on-reboot","content":"After reboot you must explicitly re-deploy."},"681":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-34","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#high-speed-interconnect","content":"No inter-node NCCL. Local multi-GPU (if advertised) uses SHM/P2P, and the `highspeed`\ninventory group is ignored."},"682":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-35","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#high-speed-interconnect","content":"**2-node pair (dual \\~400G aggregate):** existing Jobs and `group_vars` `highspeed_*` /\n`nccl_env` are **reference for a pair**. Typical env:"},"683":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-36","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#high-speed-interconnect","content":"**3-node QSFP ring (200 Gb/s per pair, triangle mesh):** used by Mode B (`glm-5.3-flash`)\nand Mode C (`deepseek-v4.1-flash`). OOB/Gloo on 10GbE (often `enP7s7`); payload on all\nfour CX-7 RoCE devices; `NCCL_NET_PLUGIN=none`. Do **not** copy the 2-node pair vars onto\nthat ring. Confirm names with `ibdev2netdev`. See LiteLLM rounded stack."},"684":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-37","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#high-speed-interconnect","content":"**4 / 5-node CRS804 switch:** each node sees **one** RoCE link — one full port per node\n(400G) for 4 nodes, or three full ports plus one port split into `sfpplus4a` / `sfpplus4b`\n(two 200G lanes) for 5. Every link is its own /24 (192.168.110–114, MTU 9000) from the\ngenerated per-node netplan. `NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME` stays the management NIC; the payload\nrides the single RoCE HCA (`NCCL_IB_HCA` from live `ibdev2netdev` names per node). Heavy\nJobs use `hostNetwork: true` — do not assume the 2-node pair `NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME` list is\ncomplete. Cabling and port map: Choose topology."},"685":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-38","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#high-speed-interconnect","content":"If NCCL payload falls back to the management network, performance will be terrible."},"686":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-39","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#high-speed-interconnect","content":"Full fabric env: Interconnect & NCCL."},"687":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-40","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#hostnetwork-and-hostipc","content":"**Omitted** (default false) on kimi / kimi-test and several 1-GPU vLLM Jobs — isolation; NCCL IFNAME still set in env."},"688":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-41","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#hostnetwork-and-hostipc","content":"**`hostNetwork: true`** on Ray, GLM-5.2, Qwen 397B, Mode B/C — ranks need the fabric NICs."},"689":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-42","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#hostnetwork-and-hostipc","content":"**`hostIPC: true`** on GLM RPC and Mode B/C ring Jobs — shared memory for TP."},"690":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-43","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#hostnetwork-and-hostipc","content":"Do not add hostNetwork to a Job “for luck”; follow the workload YAML."},"691":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-44","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#ple-mmap-qwen38-flash-next","content":"Mode A `qwen3.8-flash-next-nvfp4` requires PLE mmap (weights mapped, not fully resident). Prefix caching off. Start `max-model-len` 65536. See LiteLLM rounded stack."},"692":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-45","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#ple-mmap-qwen38-flash-next","content":"Verify interfaces on the nodes:"},"693":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-46","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#gpu-operator-on-k3s","content":"The NVIDIA GPU Operator works well on K3s but:"},"694":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-47","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#gpu-operator-on-k3s","content":"Use a recent version (v24.x+ recommended)."},"695":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-48","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#gpu-operator-on-k3s","content":"The driver container may take several minutes to load after first boot."},"696":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-49","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#gpu-operator-on-k3s","content":"On reboot, wait for `nvidia-smi` to succeed on both nodes before deploying heavy workloads."},"697":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-50","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#gpu-operator-on-k3s","content":"MIG is supported but requires explicit configuration in the ClusterPolicy."},"698":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-51","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#dual-concurrent-models-time-slicing","content":"A single GB10 exposes **one** physical GPU. To schedule two inference Jobs concurrently (e.g. Qwen3.6 dual):"},"699":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-52","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#dual-concurrent-models-time-slicing","content":"Apply `k8s/base/gpu-time-slicing` (`replicas: 2`)."},"700":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-53","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#dual-concurrent-models-time-slicing","content":"Point the device plugin at that ConfigMap (`gpu_time_slicing_enabled: true` in Ansible, or helm upgrade)."},"701":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-54","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#dual-concurrent-models-time-slicing","content":"Split memory with `--gpu-memory-utilization` (\\~0.38 each). Never run two processes at 0.9 util."},"702":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-55","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#dual-concurrent-models-time-slicing","content":"See qwen36-dual-stack.md."},"703":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-56","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#blackwell-nvfp4-kernels","content":"On DGX Spark, set `CUTE_DSL_ARCH=sm_121a`. For MoE NVFP4, use `--moe-backend flashinfer_b12x` or inference can be \\~2–2.5× slower (Marlin fallback)."},"704":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-57","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#stability-tips","content":"Reserve headroom: leave at least 10-20% of host RAM and CPU free for the system + K3s."},"705":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-58","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#stability-tips","content":"Use node affinity so that heavy inference prefers specific nodes if needed."},"706":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-59","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#stability-tips","content":"Monitor with:"},"707":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-60","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#stability-tips","content":"If SSH becomes laggy, the node is likely OOMing. Hard power cycle may be required in extreme cases."},"708":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-61","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#stability-tips","content":"Consider using `limit` equal to `request` for memory to get OOMKilled instead of silent swapping."},"709":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-62","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#recommended-workflow","content":"Start with `kimi-test` workload."},"710":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-63","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#recommended-workflow","content":"Monitor for 30-60 minutes."},"711":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-64","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#recommended-workflow","content":"Gradually increase resources in a copy of the manifest."},"712":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-65","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#recommended-workflow","content":"Only then promote to the full `kimi` version."},"713":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-66","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#recommended-workflow","content":"Always stop workloads before maintenance/reboots."},"714":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-67","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#common-failure-modes","content":"Host freezes → insufficient memory limits or too many parallel requests."},"715":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-68","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#common-failure-modes","content":"NCCL timeouts → wrong interface names or firewall rules on high-speed links."},"716":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-69","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#common-failure-modes","content":"Pods stuck in ContainerCreating → GPU Operator not fully ready."},"717":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-70","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#common-failure-modes","content":"SSH unresponsive after 10+ minutes of load → reduce concurrency or model size."},"718":{"id":"/dgx-spark-notes-71","page_id":"/dgx-spark-notes","tags":["dgx","nvidia","nccl","safety","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/dgx-spark-notes#common-failure-modes","content":"Report exact symptoms and logs when asking for help."},"719":{"id":"/getting-started","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"page","content":"Getting Started","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"url":"/getting-started"},"720":{"id":"/getting-started-0","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started","content":"Gold path — operator client, topology file, cloud-init, Ansible, GPU Operator, doctor, kimi-test, dashboard URL, and reboot reminder on 1-5 DGX Spark nodes."},"721":{"id":"/getting-started-1","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"url":"/getting-started#getting-started","content":"Getting Started"},"722":{"id":"/getting-started-2","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites"},"723":{"id":"/getting-started-3","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"Step 1 — Topology file (inventory)"},"724":{"id":"/getting-started-4","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"url":"/getting-started#step-2--cloud-init-physical-nodes","content":"Step 2 — cloud-init (physical nodes)"},"725":{"id":"/getting-started-5","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"url":"/getting-started#step-3--bootstrap-k3s","content":"Step 3 — Bootstrap K3s"},"726":{"id":"/getting-started-6","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"url":"/getting-started#step-4--gpu-operator","content":"Step 4 — GPU Operator"},"727":{"id":"/getting-started-7","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"url":"/getting-started#step-5--verify-cluster--doctor","content":"Step 5 — Verify cluster + doctor"},"728":{"id":"/getting-started-8","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"url":"/getting-started#step-6--first-safe-workload-kimi-test","content":"Step 6 — First safe workload (kimi-test)"},"729":{"id":"/getting-started-9","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"url":"/getting-started#step-7--dashboard-url","content":"Step 7 — Dashboard URL"},"730":{"id":"/getting-started-10","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"url":"/getting-started#step-8--reboot-reminder","content":"Step 8 — Reboot reminder"},"731":{"id":"/getting-started-11","page_id":"/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"url":"/getting-started#next","content":"Next"},"732":{"id":"/getting-started-12","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#getting-started","content":"**What's on this page**"},"733":{"id":"/getting-started-13","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#getting-started","content":"Prerequisites (including the one-command operator-client setup) and out-of-band console"},"734":{"id":"/getting-started-14","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#getting-started","content":"The `lab.yaml` topology file for all five configurations (1 / 2 / 3 / 4 / 5 nodes)"},"735":{"id":"/getting-started-15","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#getting-started","content":"cloud-init, Ansible bootstrap, GPU Operator"},"736":{"id":"/getting-started-16","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#getting-started","content":"`doctor`, first verify, first safe workload (`kimi-test`)"},"737":{"id":"/getting-started-17","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#getting-started","content":"Dashboard URL and reboot reminder"},"738":{"id":"/getting-started-18","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#getting-started","content":"**What this enables**"},"739":{"id":"/getting-started-19","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#getting-started","content":"A repeatable first cluster with Resource Guard and no auto-start"},"740":{"id":"/getting-started-20","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#getting-started","content":"Verification after every phase before a heavy Job"},"741":{"id":"/getting-started-21","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#getting-started","content":"Topology choice: Choose topology. Profiles after this page: Profiles."},"742":{"id":"/getting-started-22","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"1–5 DGX Spark nodes, Ubuntu 22.04 or 24.04 (fabric per node count: Choose topology)"},"743":{"id":"/getting-started-23","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"`nvidia-smi` works on the node"},"744":{"id":"/getting-started-24","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"SSH key + sudo from your workstation (operator client)"},"745":{"id":"/getting-started-25","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"**Out-of-band console** (IPMI/iDRAC) — heavy Jobs can still wedge SSH if you skip Guard"},"746":{"id":"/getting-started-26","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"Operator client (the machine that runs Ansible and `manage.sh`): Ansible ≥ 2.14, kubectl, helm, **bazelisk**"},"747":{"id":"/getting-started-27","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"One command installs and verifies everything (Homebrew, no sudo):"},"748":{"id":"/getting-started-28","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"Same script, apt/dnf based:"},"749":{"id":"/getting-started-29","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"Install WSL2 + Ubuntu once (PowerShell), then the same script inside WSL:"},"750":{"id":"/getting-started-30","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"`status` subcommand reports what is already present; see Shell reference for the full contract."},"751":{"id":"/getting-started-31","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#prerequisites","content":"Never proceed without inventory ping and OOB access. Do not start kimi / Mode B/C until `start-test` succeeds."},"752":{"id":"/getting-started-32","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"The declarative topology `ansible/inventory/lab.yaml` is the single source of truth for\n**all five configurations** — node names/IPs, fabric, switch port map, and which Spark is\nthe orchestrator. Edit it, then render:"},"753":{"id":"/getting-started-33","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"Rendering produces the Ansible inventory (`ansible/inventory/hosts.ini`, gitignored),\nfabric group vars, per-node netplan, and per-node cloud-init user-data — all from the\ntopology file. Full model: Lab topology."},"754":{"id":"/getting-started-34","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"`fabric: none`, one node with `role: orchestrator`. No high-speed cabling, local NCCL only."},"755":{"id":"/getting-started-35","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"`fabric: pair`, two nodes with both `hs_ifs` (dual QSFP direct). `group_vars` `highspeed_*`\nis the **pair** NCCL reference."},"756":{"id":"/getting-started-36","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"`fabric: ring`, three nodes, QSFP triangle. **Not** “2-node plus spark2 with pair env” —\ncabling and Job env: LiteLLM rounded stack."},"757":{"id":"/getting-started-37","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"`fabric: switch` + `switch:` block (CRS804-4DDQ-hRM `port_map`, one entry per node; 5 nodes\nuse breakout lanes `sfpplus4a`/`sfpplus4b`). Do **not** paste 2-node `NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME`\nonto switch hops without reading Interconnect & NCCL."},"758":{"id":"/getting-started-38","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"Any node may be the orchestrator — see Choose topology → Pick your orchestrator."},"759":{"id":"/getting-started-39","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"Verify:"},"760":{"id":"/getting-started-40","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"Expected: pong on every host. If not: SSH keys, management firewall, console `ip a`."},"761":{"id":"/getting-started-41","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-1--topology-file-inventory","content":"Still prefer a manual `hosts.ini`? `cp ansible/inventory/hosts.ini.example ansible/inventory/hosts.ini`\nand edit it — the classic path still works, it just skips the generated netplan / cloud-init."},"762":{"id":"/getting-started-42","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-2--cloud-init-physical-nodes","content":"Render early OS / highspeed user-data **before** or as the first part of bootstrap."},"763":{"id":"/getting-started-43","page_id":"/getting-started","tags":["getting-started","bazel","k3s","ansible","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/getting-started#step-2--cloud-init-physical-nodes","content":"With a `lab.yaml` in place, user-data is generated per node at\